#!/usr/bin/env bash
# commit-msg — refuse a commit message whose subject carries no known type prefix,
# then require a task number (or a traced `Sans-tache:`) by threshold: warning
# below it, refusal above it (see THE TASK NUMBER below).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. `AGENTS.md` § Conventions lists seven commit types and nothing
# read them. Measured 2026-09-14 while taking the relevé T-00000593 asks for:
# `core.hooksPath` is `.githooks`, that directory held ONLY `pre-push`, and no
# `commit-msg` existed anywhere in the tree. The convention was held by memory
# alone — which is the whole point of that ticket.
#
# WHY THIS ONE IS MECHANISABLE WHEN MOST OF ITS SIBLINGS ARE NOT. T-00000593's
# design rule is "what DETERMINISTIC ARTEFACT would exist if the rule had been
# followed, and who can observe it". Here the artefact IS the thing being judged:
# the commit message. There is no self-declared marker in the loop, so the usual
# objection — an agent that posts its own proof proves nothing — does not apply.
#
# WHAT IT IS, AND THE WORD MATTERS, exactly as `pre-push` says of itself: a local
# REMINDER, not a gate. `git commit --no-verify` skips it entirely, and it only
# runs at all where `core.hooksPath` points here. It ATTESTS a convention; it
# PROVES nothing about a forge.
#
# IT JUDGES FORM, NEVER TRUTH. `feat:` on a pure deletion passes. That bound is
# deliberate and is the same one the rest of this kit writes down: a hook can
# never invoke a model, so nothing here can weigh whether the type fits the diff.
# Saying so is part of the contract — a guard whose limits are unwritten gets
# read as covering more than it does.
#
# THE KNOWN HOLES ARE BOUNDED, NOT ENUMERATED: `--no-verify`, a hook never
# installed, and every commit made through a path that bypasses hooks. Two more
# are NAMED because they were MEASURED rather than imagined, and the first draft
# of this header got one of them exactly backwards:
#
#   * `git merge -m "<anything>"` — MERGE_HEAD is set, so the subject the
#     COMMITTER chose is never judged. The first draft blamed `--amend` instead;
#     measured, an `--amend --no-edit` IS judged and an amend that rewrites a
#     subject is judged too. Naming the wrong hole is worse than naming none:
#     it sends the reader to guard a door that is already shut.
#   * A FIRST LINE THAT IS A COMMENT, on the `-m` / `-F` path. Those use
#     `--cleanup=whitespace`, which KEEPS comments, so git records `#` as the
#     subject while this hook skips it and reads the next line. Measured:
#     `git commit -m "$(printf '#\nfix: x')"` is accepted and stores `#` as the
#     subject. Closing it means making this hook model git's cleanup modes,
#     which is a bigger mechanism than the one it guards; the divergence is
#     pinned by an arm of the bench instead of being fixed, and reopening it is
#     a decision, not a patch.
#
# THE EDITOR PATH HANDS THIS HOOK THE UNCLEANED FILE. An earlier header said
# git strips its template before this hook runs; REFUTED 2026-10-19 (git
# 2.54.0): under `git commit -v` the file received here carries the `#`
# template, then `# ------------------------ >8 ------------------------`, then
# the STAGED DIFF. The task-number check below therefore reads only the lines
# ABOVE the first line that ENDS with ` ------------------------ >8 ---...`
# (whatever its comment prefix) and skips `#` lines: a `T-...` in the diff
# never satisfies it.
#
# THE TASK NUMBER (T-01M54GEQ68NTP1C34EYTF0SDHX), JUDGED AFTER THE TYPE AND AFTER
# EVERY EXEMPTION. A typed message must also carry a task number — `T-` then 3
# to 15 digits or 10 to 26 ULID characters, on a non-`#` line above the cut — or
# a TRACED way out, a line `Sans-tache: <why>` with at least 10 non-blank
# characters. Without one, the verdict depends on a THRESHOLD (palier) recomputed
# at every commit, with no state and no switch: among the 200 last non-merge
# commits of HEAD, those whose subject is not `chore(state): ` / `chore(runs): `
# are ELIGIBLE (N); those that pass the very predicate above are CONFORMING (K).
# N < 20 or K < 95 % of N: a WARNING, rc 0. Otherwise: REFUSED, rc 1. Once
# refusing, every commit that passes is conforming — a ratchet in fact.
# Bounds, SAID: the threshold reads HEAD's history, not the clone's (a commit
# made with `--no-verify` or without the hook counts against it); a cut line
# written by hand on `-m`/`-F` truncates the reading — stricter, never wider;
# `core.commentChar`/`core.commentString` other than `#` makes the template
# read as text (a listed path `docs/tasks/T-...` would satisfy the rule;
# measured unset here); the FORM of the number is judged, never its existence
# on the board.
#
# INSTALLING IT: the same single gesture as `pre-push`, and it carries the same
# warning — `core.hooksPath` REPLACES `.git/hooks/` in its entirety rather than
# adding to it. See the header of `.githooks/pre-push` before running:
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks
# That one gesture also arms its two siblings, `.githooks/post-merge` and
# `.githooks/post-commit`: they ALERT (stderr, never a refusal, always rc 0)
# when a merge touched a `merge=cadre-enregistrement` path while this clone's
# field-merge driver is missing or invalid. Their bounds are written in the
# header of `.githooks/post-merge`. Nothing below depends on them.

set -u

MSG_FILE="${1:-}"
if [ -z "$MSG_FILE" ] || [ ! -f "$MSG_FILE" ]; then
  # No message file is not our business to adjudicate: git is mid-something we
  # do not model. Fail OPEN, like every advisory surface in this kit.
  exit 0
fi

# The subject is the FIRST NON-COMMENT, NON-EMPTY line. Reading line 1 blindly
# would judge the leading blank line of a `-F -` message, and would judge a
# comment on a template. Neither is the subject git will record.
SUBJECT=""
line=""
# `|| [ -n "$line" ]` KEEPS THE LAST LINE WHEN THE FILE HAS NO TRAILING NEWLINE.
# Without it `read` returns false on that line and the loop body never runs, so a
# one-line message with no final newline produced an EMPTY subject and sailed
# through the whole hook. Caught by arm 3a of the bench the day this was written,
# which is the entire reason that arm exists.
while IFS= read -r line || [ -n "$line" ]; do
  case "$line" in
    "#"*)
      continue
      ;;
    "")
      continue
      ;;
    *)
      SUBJECT="$line"
      break
      ;;
  esac
done < "$MSG_FILE"

# An empty message aborts the commit on git's own account — saying anything here
# would put a convention error in front of a user who is already being refused.
if [ -z "$SUBJECT" ]; then
  exit 0
fi

# --- LE NUMERO DE TACHE ET SON PALIER : DEFINITIONS (voir l en-tete) ---------
# Definies ICI, avant les exemptions, et INERTES : rien n est juge avant l appel
# qui suit le controle du type, plus bas.
TAB="$(printf '\t')"
COUPE=' ------------------------ >8 ------------------------'
RE_NUM='(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_-])T-([0-9]{3,15}|[0-9A-HJKMNP-TV-Z]{10,26})([^A-Za-z0-9]|$)'
RE_SANS="^[0-9]+${TAB}Sans-tache:([[:blank:]]*[^[:blank:]]){10}"

# corps <exclure> : lit des messages dont chacun OUVRE par l octet \001 ; ecrit
# « n<TAB> » une fois par message retenu, puis « n<TAB><ligne> » par ligne LUE —
# arret a la ligne de coupe, lignes `#` sautees. exclure=1 ecarte les messages
# `chore(state): ` / `chore(runs): ` (le palier) ; 0 les garde (le message en
# cours, qui doit porter son numero comme les autres). UNE fonction pour les
# deux usages : le palier compte EXACTEMENT le predicat d acceptation unitaire.
corps() {
  LC_ALL=C awk -v exclure="$1" -v coupe="$COUPE" '
    BEGIN { n = 0; garde = 0; coupee = 0; lc = length(coupe) }
    substr($0, 1, 1) == "\001" {
      n++
      $0 = substr($0, 2)
      coupee = 0
      garde = 1
      if (exclure == 1 && (index($0, "chore(state): ") == 1 || index($0, "chore(runs): ") == 1)) garde = 0
      if (garde) print n "\t"
    }
    !garde || coupee { next }
    length($0) >= lc && substr($0, length($0) - lc + 1) == coupe { coupee = 1; next }
    substr($0, 1, 1) == "#" { next }
    { print n "\t" $0 }
  '
}

# Les lignes « n<TAB>... » qui portent un numero ou une sortie `Sans-tache:`.
lignes_porteuses() {
  LC_ALL=C grep -E -e "$RE_NUM" -e "$RE_SANS"
}

message_en_cours() {
  printf '\001'
  cat -- "$MSG_FILE"
}

porte_numero() {
  [ -n "$(message_en_cours | corps 0 | lignes_porteuses)" ]
}

formes_acceptees() {
  printf 'Formes acceptees (une seule suffit) :\n'
  printf '  fix(x): le sujet (T-<id>)\n'
  printf '  une ligne de corps : Tâche: T-<id>\n'
  printf '  git commit -m "<sujet>" -m "Sans-tache: <pourquoi, 10 caracteres au moins>"\n'
  printf '    (sortie TRACEE, comptee par tracabilite.py bilan)\n'
  printf 'T-<id> : 3 a 15 chiffres, ou 10 a 26 caracteres d un ULID (prefixe compris).\n'
}

# Toujours une sortie : avertissement rc 0, ou refus rc 1. Calcule seulement
# quand le message n a PAS de numero.
juger_palier() {
  HIST="$(git -c log.showSignature=false log --no-merges -n 200 --format='%x01%B' HEAD 2>/dev/null | corps 1)"
  N="$(printf '%s\n' "$HIST" | cut -f1 | LC_ALL=C sort -u | grep -c .)"
  K="$(printf '%s\n' "$HIST" | lignes_porteuses | cut -f1 | LC_ALL=C sort -u | grep -c .)"
  if [ "$N" -lt 20 ] || [ $((K * 100)) -lt $((N * 95)) ]; then
    {
      printf 'AVERTISSEMENT commit-msg : aucun numéro de tâche — palier %s/%s sous 95 %% (ou moins de 20 éligibles) ; ce commit sera REFUSÉ dès que 95 %% des commits éligibles parmi les 200 derniers commits hors fusion en portent un.\n' "$K" "$N"
      printf '\n'
      formes_acceptees
    } >&2
    exit 0
  fi
  {
    printf 'REFUSE par commit-msg : aucun numéro de tâche.\n'
    printf '\n'
    printf '  sujet lu : %s\n' "$SUBJECT"
    printf '  palier %s/%s : 95 %% au moins des commits éligibles parmi les 200 derniers commits hors fusion portent un numéro, le refus est en vigueur.\n' "$K" "$N"
    printf '\n'
    formes_acceptees
    printf '\n'
    printf 'Ce hook juge la FORME du numero, jamais son existence au board.\n'
  } >&2
  exit 1
}

# THE EXEMPTIONS, AND EACH ONE IS A MESSAGE GIT AUTHORS ITSELF OR REWRITES LATER.
# Refusing these would make the hook fire on gestures whose subject is not the
# committer's to choose — the profile that gets a guard disabled within the week.
# `Merge ` ET `Revert ` ETAIENT DES MOTS LIBRES, ET LE REFUS IMPRIMAIT SON
# PROPRE CONTOURNEMENT. Mesure : « Merge les deux configs sans type » et
# « Revert le chantier entier » passaient tous deux, et le texte du refus
# ENUMERAIT les prefixes exemptes — un lecteur refuse n avait qu a recopier le
# premier. Les motifs ci-dessous sont les formes que git ECRIT vraiment, et les
# vraies fusions restent de toute facon couvertes par MERGE_HEAD plus bas.
case "$SUBJECT" in
  "Merge branch "*|"Merge branches "*|"Merge remote-tracking branch "*|"Merge tag "*|"Merge commit "*|"Merge pull request "*|'Revert "'*|"fixup! "*|"squash! "*|"amend! "*|"Squashed commit of the following:"*)
    exit 0
    ;;
esac

# A rebase or a cherry-pick replays subjects that were already judged when they
# were first written. Judging them again turns one old miss into a wall that
# stops an unrelated operation.
GIT_DIR_PATH="$(git rev-parse --git-dir 2>/dev/null)" || GIT_DIR_PATH=""
if [ -n "$GIT_DIR_PATH" ]; then
  # REVERT_HEAD VOYAGE AVEC LE RESSERREMENT CI-DESSUS, et pas separement : tant
  # que « Revert » etait un mot libre, un `git revert` etait couvert par le
  # prefixe. Maintenant que le prefixe exige la forme exacte de git, un revert
  # d un commit dont le sujet d origine n avait pas de type serait refuse sans
  # ce marqueur. Les deux corrections sont une seule.
  for marker in rebase-merge rebase-apply CHERRY_PICK_HEAD REVERT_HEAD MERGE_HEAD; do
    if [ -e "$GIT_DIR_PATH/$marker" ]; then
      exit 0
    fi
  done
fi

# The ten types of `AGENTS.md` § Conventions, and nothing else. An optional
# `(scope)` and an optional `!` for a breaking change are accepted because both
# are Conventional Commits and both already appear in this repo's history.
#
# TEN AND NOT SEVEN — DECISION PILOTE DU 2026-09-14, PRISE SUR UNE MESURE. The
# doctrine listed seven; the history uses three more. Measured over all 1065
# subjects: 1054 conform (99,0 %), and of the eleven that do not, `ci:` appears
# three times, `build(ui):` and `revert(atterrissage):` once each — types
# Conventional Commits defines and this repo already writes. Refusing them would
# have taught the `--no-verify` reflex on the very gestures a repo makes most
# often, which is how a guard gets disabled in the week. `AGENTS.md` moved in
# the same commit: the hook and the doctrine never travel apart.
TYPES="feat|fix|chore|docs|refactor|perf|test|revert|ci|build"

# LE TYPE EST BON : le numero de tache est juge ICI, apres les exemptions et
# les marqueurs, jamais avant (bras 10f du banc, mutant M-H4).
if printf '%s' "$SUBJECT" | grep -qE "^($TYPES)(\([^)]+\))?!?: .+"; then
  if porte_numero; then
    exit 0
  fi
  juger_palier
fi

# THE REFUSAL CONTRACT HERE IS GIT'S, NOT THIS KIT'S PER-HOST HOOK CONTRACT:
# stderr plus a non-zero exit, with the remedy printed. No host registry is
# involved and none is touched — this is a git hook, not an agent-host hook.
{
  printf 'REFUSE par commit-msg : le sujet ne porte aucun type connu.\n'
  printf '\n'
  printf '  sujet lu : %s\n' "$SUBJECT"
  printf '\n'
  printf 'Les dix types de AGENTS.md, section Conventions :\n'
  printf '  feat:  fix:  chore:  docs:  refactor:  perf:  test:\n'
  printf '  revert:  ci:  build:\n'
  printf '\n'
  printf 'Formes acceptees, portee et rupture comprises :\n'
  printf '  fix: le sujet\n'
  printf '  fix(dash): le sujet\n'
  printf '  feat(porte)!: le sujet\n'
  printf '\n'
  printf 'Les fusions, reverts et fixup/squash/amend ECRITS PAR GIT sont deja\n'
  printf 'exemptes, ainsi que tout commit joue pendant un rebase, un cherry-pick,\n'
  printf 'un revert ou une fusion. Tu n as rien a faire pour eux.\n'
  printf '\n'
  printf 'Ce hook juge la FORME, jamais la verite : il ne sait pas si le type\n'
  printf 'colle au diff, et il ne peut pas le savoir — aucun hook de ce depot\n'
  printf 'n invoque de modele.\n'
} >&2

exit 1
